  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "x6ea4xr",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2.1 Definition and Scope of Agronomy"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Agronomy encompasses definition, classification of crops, and sustainable cropping systems.",
        "Planned crop rotation provides crucial soil health and yield benefits.",
        "Primary Indian field crops include Rice (Oryza sativa), Wheat (Triticum aestivum), Maize (Zea mays), and Sugarcane (Saccharum officinarum).",
        "Seed technology relies on distinct seed classes, rigorous quality parameters, and proper seed treatments.",
        "Water management focuses on identifying and supplying water during critical irrigation stages."
      ],
      "id": "zalrtt1"
    },
